xnu 0147: run the bit-bang as fast as the pads allow, and time the frame

Android proves the part answers the same confirm: the working driver logs
"brl_dev_confirm: device connected" and its chip_info reads rom_pid BERLIN,
config_version 46. It talks over the QUP at up to 15 MHz; this driver clocks
at about 0.6 MHz, and a slave with a transfer timeout would drop a frame that
slow.

Drop the artificial delays (half period 0) and measure the real frame time
with the timebase, so the log says how fast the pads actually go. Two tries
each at 600 kHz, 2.5 MHz, 10 MHz and as fast as the writes allow.

